{
  "_fixture": {
    "ticket": "TEAM-4760 U4",
    "what": "Hand-built inputs for the ten deterministic SI metrics (si_metrics.py). NOT a captured window — every card, ledger, analysis and workflow row exists to pin one branch: the v6 read, the v5 (None, reason) read, a duplicated merge commit, a clean one, the coverage ratio, the recurrence rate. No real window contains all of those at once. The two events-based cases that ARE real live in sffzti-dossier.json / yteqfl-dossier.json; only the synthetic gap run below is hand-built, because neither real run has a missed rewake.",
    "readBy": [
      "deploy/workflow-manager/toolkit/test_si_metrics.py — FakeSource serves cards/events/cdLedgers/analyses/workflows/ledgerRows straight out of this file, one happy-path test per metric plus the v6-only unavailable paths"
    ],
    "windows": {
      "all": "{defIds:[software-delivery], since:2026-09-01T00:00:00Z, until:2026-09-14T00:00:00Z} — all three cards, all four terminal software-delivery runs, all four analyses",
      "v6": "{defIds:[software-delivery], since:2026-09-09T00:00:00Z} — wf_si_a + wf_si_b only (the v5 card completed 2026-09-08)",
      "v5": "{defIds:[software-delivery], since:2026-09-07T00:00:00Z, until:2026-09-09T00:00:00Z} — wf_si_v5 only, the window that must produce (None, reason) for the three #635 metrics",
      "bugfix": "{defIds:[bug-fix], since:2026-09-01T00:00:00Z} — the two REAL dossier runs, for missed_rewake_gaps"
    },
    "cases": {
      "cards.wf_si_a": "reportVersion 6 (post-#635). quality.errors is the BY-KIND object {agent.error:1, agent.retry:2, agent.died:1} → dead_sessions 3; quality.rewakes 5; quality.reinvocations.byKind.ci_recert 2; plus the v5 fields reworkRounds 4 and interventions 3. Also carries interventionsDetail, so a reader of the v6 shape sees the whole of it.",
      "cards.wf_si_b": "reportVersion 6, deliberately smaller numbers than wf_si_a (errors agent.retry 1 / agent.died 0 → dead_sessions 1; rewakes 3; ci_recert 4; reworkRounds 2; interventions 1) so every per-run mean over {a,b} is a value neither card has on its own: dead 2.0, rewakes 4.0, ci_recert 3.0, rework 3.0.",
      "cards.wf_si_v5": "reportVersion 5 — exactly the quality block lambda/cost-report/index.mjs emits on main: errors is a NUMBER (2), retries 1, unblocks 9, NO rewakes, NO reinvocations, NO interventionsDetail. This is the card that proves dead_sessions_per_run / rewakes_per_run / ci_recerts_per_run return (None, reason) naming reportVersion 5 and PR #635, while rework_rounds_v2 (6) and wm_interventions_per_run (4) still read fine.",
      "events.wf_si_gaps": "Six tickets, one synthetic run, three gaps over the 60 s threshold. TEAM-9001 unblocked 07:00:00 → invoked 07:06:00 (360 s, COUNTED). TEAM-9002 unblocked 07:10:00 → invoked 07:11:30 (90 s, COUNTED). TEAM-9003 unblocked 07:20:00 → invoked 07:20:10 (10 s, under threshold). TEAM-9004 INVOKED 07:30:00.000 then unblocked 07:30:02.800 — the real publish order of one dispatch (the yteqfl fixture shows leads up to 2.8 s), so it is a gap of 0, not a miss. TEAM-9005 unblocked 07:40:00 and never invoked — a human gate, deliberately NOT counted. TEAM-9006 two rounds: 07:45:00 → 07:45:05 (5 s, under threshold) and 08:00:00 → 08:02:00 (120 s, COUNTED), which is what makes the greedy per-ticket pairing observable.",
      "events.wf_si_gaps.duplicates": "TEAM-9001's unblock + invoke and TEAM-9002's unblock each appear TWICE — the direct PutItem and the EventBridge fan-out copy (`source: agentcore-hub.orchestrator`, different eventId, second-granularity row timestamp, reordered detail keys), exactly as the live events table holds them. Without events.dedupe_events the run scores 4 gaps instead of 3.",
      "cdLedgers.wf_si_a": "The DOUBLE-DEPLOY: an `executions` list where merge commit a1b2c3d4 has two execution ids and e5f6a7b8 has one → 1 extra execution.",
      "cdLedgers.wf_si_b": "The clean single-object ledger today's release manager writes ({pipeline, executionId, mergeCommit, prUrl, approvedHeadSha, gateTicketId}) → 0 extras. Mean over {a,b} = 0.5.",
      "cdLedgers.wf_si_gaps": "ABSENT from this map, as is wf_si_v5 (a definite 404) — neither run deployed, so they contribute nothing rather than a zero. Two of the four terminal runs therefore contribute, which is what the result's `runs: 2` proves.",
      "cdLedgers.wf_si_superseded": "Single-object ledger plus priorExecutionIds — a superseded execution re-triggered on the same merge commit → 1 extra. Read by the pure-function test only (no workflow row), since no real window mixes it with the others.",
      "cdLedgers.wf_si_noexec": "A ledger with an empty executionId → None (nothing to count), never 0. Pure-function test only.",
      "analyses.an_a1": "wf_si_a, analyzedAt 2026-09-10T19:00:00Z, metrics.humanWaitOutsideHoursMs 7200000 — SUPERSEDED by an_a2.",
      "analyses.an_a2": "wf_si_a re-analysed 2026-09-13T08:00:00Z with 5400000 — the latest analysis per run is the one that counts, so the mean uses 5400000, not 7200000.",
      "analyses.an_b1": "wf_si_b, 3600000. Mean over {a,b} = 4500000 ms.",
      "analyses.an_v5": "wf_si_v5, metrics with NO humanWaitOutsideHoursMs (analysed before the TEAM-4453 in/out-of-hours split existed) → skipped, never read as 0. It still counts for analysis_coverage (the run WAS analysed) and for the recurrence denominator.",
      "workflows": "Four terminal software-delivery runs (wf_si_a, wf_si_b, wf_si_v5 as static-ci-only, wf_si_gaps) → analysis_coverage denominator 4, numerator 3 (wf_si_gaps was never analysed) = 0.75. wf_si_running (phase running) and wf_si_deleted (deleted:true) must be filtered out by the source, not by the metric. The two real dossier runs carry their own real phases/completedAt under defId bug-fix.",
      "ledgerRows.rewake-gap-after-unblock": "Three DATED occurrences inside the `all` window against four analyses → 3/4 × 10 = 7.5 per 10 analyses.",
      "ledgerRows.ci-recert-storm": "`occurrences` is a bare count (5). Windowed → unavailable: an all-time count over a 14-day denominator is not a windowed rate.",
      "ledgerRows.undated-occurrence": "A dated-list row with one undated entry → unavailable when a window bound is given, because that entry can be neither included nor excluded."
    }
  },

